'''Medal King''' is a [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cat]] that can be obtained from the [[Download Celebration! (Event Gacha)|Download Celebration!]] Event Gacha. He was added in [[Version 13.0 Update|Version 13.0]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 726
|rarity = EX
|name1 = Medal King
|name2 = Medal Emperor
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Medal Emperor''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Medal King can be treated as an arguably worse version of [[Slug Jockey Cat (Rare Cat)|Slug Jockey Cat]]. The two share range and fairly low overall stats, however Slug Jockey has [[Area Attack]], faster attack rate, shorter foreswing, quicker speed, lower cost and shorter recharge. The only real advantage this unit has is a [[Surge Attack]], which doesn't increase the slow uptime enough to be worthwhile. In fact, Medal King's Surge and slightly better damage actually work against him, making it harder to stack him on peons like Slug Jockey can.

Medal King's slow is just too short to make any impact, and may even make things worse if used in conjunction with other [[:Category:Cats with Slow ability|slowers]]. For example, if [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Crystal Cat]] slows an enemy, and then Medal King hits that same enemy, the enemy will be slowed for 1 second instead of 10 seconds. Even if the surge hits a backliner enemy, it won't have much impact. Backliner enemies usually rely on high damage or abilities to make things tough for the cats, neither of which slow can prevent, unlike [[Weaken]] or [[Freeze]].

