==Trivia==
*Medal King was originally unlocked through the [[Medal King's Palace (Event Gacha)|Medal King's Palace]] Event Gacha.
*Medal King and the Small Medals used to play the Medal King's Palace Gacha reference the ''[[wikipedia:Dragon Quest|Dragon Quest]]'' series' [https://dragon-quest.org/wiki/Medal_King Medal Kings] and the [https://dragon-quest.org/wiki/Mini_medal Mini medals] they collect. In particular, Medal King resembles Medford, the Medal King from ''[https://dragon-quest.org/wiki/Dragon_Quest_VI:_Realms_of_Revelation Dragon Quest VI: Realms of Revelation]''. The Small Medals and Mini medals' names are arguably more similar in Japanese, with the former being 伝説のちいさいメダル ''Densetsu no Chiisai Medaru'' and the latter ちいさなメダル ''Chiisana Medaru''.
*Medal Emperor's sword bears some similarities to [https://dragon-quest.org/wiki/Erdrick's_Sword Erdrick's Sword] from the ''Dragon Quest'' series, particularly the hilt.
*The 11 years and 11 trillion yen in his Japanese descriptions are, of course, referring to how Medal King was released during the 11th anniversary.

